# Trello control-plane activation (opt-in). Copy this file to
# config/trello.env in your firstmate home and fill in the three values.
# config/trello.env is gitignored - NEVER commit a real token.
#
# The control plane is a HARD no-op until all three keys below are present, so a
# user who never creates this file sees zero behavior change (same gate as X mode's
# .env). See docs/trello-control-plane.md for the full activation and poll model.
#
# api.trello.com is an EXTERNAL host: firstmate reaches it only when this file is
# present. The CLI and the Atlassian gateway cannot post comments, so the control
# plane talks to the REST API directly, authed with the key/token below.

# Your Trello API key. Get one from https://trello.com/power-ups/admin (create a
# Power-Up, then read its API key), or the legacy https://trello.com/app-key.
TRELLO_API_KEY=

# A user token authorizing that key to read and write your board. Generate it
# from the API key page's "Token" link; grant read + write scope.
TRELLO_TOKEN=

# The short link (the code in the board URL: trello.com/b/<THIS>/my-board), not
# the full 24-char board id. Lane list ids are resolved dynamically from the
# board at runtime, so only the board itself is configured here.
TRELLO_BOARD_SHORTLINK=

# Optional: override the API base (developers pointing at a mock only).
# TRELLO_API_BASE=https://api.trello.com
